I would close the WireGuard task properly and start RDP audio as a new task at stage 0, in parallel. Operator-facing text is in Russian (§15, ruling 2026-09-21); a short English gloss follows each.

## 1. Read-only checks — Bash, foreground

```bash
REPO=~/work/ccs.ansible; S=<orchestrator scratch>; INBOX=$S/inbox
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent list                                   # wgka idle; note its tab_id
git -C $REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain   # must print nothing
git -C $REPO fetch origin && git -C $REPO branch --merged origin/main | grep -F feat/wg-keepalive-relay
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command                         # still my codex app-server broker?
codex plugin list </dev/null | grep -F superpowers
claude plugin list | grep -F superpowers
```

## 2. Backlog — Write, Bash foreground, Artifact tool

Two rows in `$S/orchestrator/backlog.md`:

```
| wgka | WireGuard keepalive relay | docs closed | main | <spec path> | feat/wg-keepalive-relay / #165 merged | close docs, then cleanup | — | operator 2026-09-28 23:10 "accepted", ping 0% loss | no: snapshot, living docs, spec/plan status, memory |
| rdpa | RDP audio | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | — | — | round 1: independent drafts | — | operator 2026-09-28 23:10 "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." | no |
```

Then `bash $S/orchestrator/build-backlog.sh` (foreground) and an Artifact update at the same page path.

## 3. WireGuard docs — Bash foreground, Write, Agent tool

```bash
git -C $REPO worktree add $REPO/.claude/worktrees/wgka-docs -b chore/wgka-docs-close origin/main
```

I write `$S/wgka/evidence.md` from my own deploy log, read-only verification, the `changed=0` re-run and the operator's pasted ping summary. Then Agent tool, `model: opus`, background:

```
You are a prose subagent of the orchestrator. Reply in English. No decisions, no host access.
TASK      wgka — close the docs of the WireGuard keepalive relay
DIR       <abs path>/.claude/worktrees/wgka-docs   branch chore/wgka-docs-close   base origin/main
EVIDENCE  <S>/wgka/evidence.md — the only source of live-state facts
WRITE     1) projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md  2) living docs that lag the merged code
          3) the task's spec and plan: "implemented — PR #165; canary ccs-it accepted
             2026-09-28; ccs-ops not rolled out"
MUST NOT  state anything the evidence does not show; predict a result; touch soul/ccs-ops.md;
          change CLAUDE.md "Hard rules", "Git / PR workflow", "Conventions" or
          docs/orchestration.md; change a non-Markdown file; add a session link; push
COMMIT    local only, Co-Authored-By trailer only
REPORT    files changed, head SHA, the evidence line behind every sentence added, PR title + body
```

## 4. RDP audio, stage 0 — two new tabs

`wgka` gets no message. Bash, foreground:

```bash
mkdir -p $S/brainstorm/codex/rdp-audio $S/brainstorm/fable/rdp-audio
P1=$(herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm/codex --label prod-codex --no-focus | jq -r .result.root_pane.pane_id)
P2=$(herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm/fable --label prod-fable --no-focus | jq -r .result.root_pane.pane_id)
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane $P1 --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane $P2 --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
herdr agent get prod-codex; herdr agent get prod-fable      # focused must be false
```

Brief, saved as `$S/brainstorm/brief-rdpa-r1-<codex|fable>.txt`:

```
You are product advisor <A|B> in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       rdpa — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file exists and you have reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go."
FACTS      F1 That sentence is the whole requirement.
           F2 RDP as designed: docs/v3/30-rdp.md, docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-21-ccs-rdp-lan-ccs-password-design.md;
              CLAUDE.md (rdp_server, "Gateway VM (v4)") records audio as out of scope, "phase 2".
           F3 No host evidence exists for this task. Name the fact you need; I collect it.
DECIDED    CLAUDE.md hard rules #1–#18 as written (note #1, #2, #7, #9, #11, #14, #17);
           canary is ccs-it. "Never target `site_host` or `65.21.207.111`."
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      rdp-audio/draft-<codex|fable>.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal; draft
           nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   45 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

Two Bash calls, each **background**:

```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $S/brainstorm/brief-rdpa-r1-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $INBOX/prod-codex.last
```

The second call is the same for `prod-fable`.

